[Music]  in recent years Disney has unveiled  culturally diverse princesses to its  lineup but for those who crave even more  diversity these altered photos created  by a talented artist named titi of the  tumblr vlog  let there be doodles will amaze you if  you're new to our channel don't forget  to subscribe and please give this video  a big thumbs up because today we'll be  sharing 10 alternate stories of Disney  Princesses in other countries just wait  until you see the new version of  Princess Jasmine it's guaranteed to  shock you Cinderella we definitely did a  double-take when we saw this alternate  version of Cinderella the characters  European features are long gone she's  now turned into a Geisha a traditional  Japanese female entertainer her rags  have been converted into a beautiful  kimono and an Obi tied around her waist  she also wears the traditional white  makeup that covers her entire face and  neck Aurora we're all used to seeing  Princess Aurora look like this and  that's why we're absolutely floored when  we saw her brand new look the original  Aurora has fair skin blond hair and  violet eyes now take a look at the  Jamaican version of the Sleeping Beauty  character her skin is golden brown and  she wears her hair in traditional  dreadlocks would you watch a Jamaican  version of this film let us know down  below Elsa Elsa may be from arendelle  but in the artist TT's rendition she's  transformed into a Mexican princess  their frozen character wears antique  gold jewelry encrusted with rubies and a  traditional floral headdress with  cascading flowers adorning her dark hair  how beautiful do you think she looks let  us know if you prefer the original Elsa  or her new look in the comment section  Pocahontas Pocahontas has been  captivating Disney fans ever since the  1995 release of the film with her long  dark hair and dark features we didn't  think this Native American princess  could get any more beautiful but she  just did check out this photo of the  artist's rendition of a Pacific Islander  version of the princess her  eyes are much whiter her nose is broader  and she has some fabulous beachy waves  in her hair to complete her look a red  hibiscus flower sits behind her ear  snow-white the original Snow White is a  German character with light skin and  dark hair and eyes but check out this  brand-new version of the Disney Princess  Snow White is now a Latina woman with  olive skin  she wears a festive red dress with  ruffles on the shoulders and her hair is  styled in an updo with a flower pinned  to the side to pay homage to Latin  folklore Megara Megara the wife of  Hercules is a stunning Greek beauty but  the character went through a total  transformation to become an ancient  Egyptian in this picture you can see  just how much mcGarry's features and  clothing have been changed to fit in  with traditional Egyptian attire the  ancient Egyptians would wear lavish  jewellery to signify their wealth and  the updated version of Megara is  dripping in jewels she wears a gold  headdress gold earrings in a traditional  gold armband and we can't get enough of  her new makeup how gorgeous does she  look with her darkly rimmed eyes and  teal eye shadow jasmine Aladdin's  Princess Jasmine continues to wow us  with her good looks her flawless hair  and her dazzling outfits but check out  her now the character from the Arabian  city of Agrabah is now a Kenyan princess  jasmine has been transformed into a  Masai woman complete with traditional  face paint beaded jewelry and a colorful  headband even Jasmine's tiger Raja is  transformed into a lion which is a  symbol of Kenya's nationhood Tiana their  world rejoiced when Disney revealed its  first african-american princess tiana  and now the new orleans character has  been revamped to fit into a brand new  culture as an East Asian princess her  eyes were widened and lengthened and  when it comes to her hair it's styled in  a traditional bun do you think it's  about time Disney created an East Asian  princess let us know what you think down  in the comments section Belle Belle is  gorgeous in her own right but we love  this alternate version of The Beauty and  the Beast star and this photo Belle is  transformed into a beautiful Muslim  woman her  skin and her hair have been darkened to  give her a warm glow and she's wearing a  hijab which is a traditional Muslim head  covering wouldn't it be awesome to see a  Muslim version of Beauty and the Beast  Arielle everyone's favorite mermaid just  got a brand new look Ariel's red hair  and blue eyes are long gone and she has  now been recreated as an Indian princess  she wears a gold and purple mang tika in  her hair and a gold nose ring a red  bindi on her forehead and she has a  henna tattoo on her hand do you think  area looks better in her original form  or as an Indian princess which of these  artists recreations of the Disney  Princesses from different cultures did  you love the most  let us know in the comments section and  the most original reply will be pinned  to our channel if you'd like to see more  videos like this don't forget to  subscribe to our channel and give this  video a big thumbs up  [Music]

